From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Date: Sun, 3 Aug 2026 22:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: Set in_gpu_reset for GMUX runtime resume

The GMUX power-off is a hard D3cold with complete VRAM loss.  The
default runtime-resume path (from_suspend=false) assumes PSP firmware
is still present in VRAM, causing "PSP load kdb failed" after resume.

Set in_gpu_reset=true for the GMUX runtime mode so amdgpu performs a
full GPU init including PSP firmware reload.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
index 603ff39aada4..a72c0a9b3e4f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
@@ -2951,6 +2951,8 @@ static int amdgpu_pmops_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 			pci_disable_device(pdev);
 		return ret;
 	}
+	if (adev->pm.rpm_mode == AMDGPU_RUNPM_GMUX)
+		adev->in_gpu_reset = true;
 	ret = amdgpu_device_resume(drm_dev, false);
 	if (ret) {
 		if (adev->pm.rpm_mode == AMDGPU_RUNPM_PX ||
-- 
2.55.0
